{"name":"Toad King","hex":"#3d6c54","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"toad","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An amphibian, a kind of frog (broad sense, order Anura) with shorter hindlegs and a drier, wartier skin, many in family Bufonidae.","A contemptible or unpleasant person."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To expel (a user) permanently from a MUD or similar system, so that their account is deleted."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toad"},{"term":"king","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male monarch; a man who heads a monarchy; in an absolute monarchy, the supreme ruler of his nation.","The monarch with the most power and authority in a monarchy, regardless of sex."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To crown king, to make (a person) king.","To rule over as king."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/king"}],"entries":[{"title":"Toad","blocks":[{"text":"Toad is a generic common name for certain groups of frogs, especially those of the family Bufonidae, that are characterized by short legs and dry, leathery skin with large bumps made of the parotoid glands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Bombina_bombina_1_%28Marek_Szczepanek%29.jpg/330px-Bombina_bombina_1_%28Marek_Szczepanek%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toad"},{"title":"King","blocks":[{"text":"King is a royal title given to a male monarch. A king is an absolute monarch if he holds unrestricted governmental power or exercises full sovereignty over a nation. In a modern context, the title may refer to the ruler of one of a number of modern monarchies. The title of king is used alongside other titles for monarchs: in the West, emperor, grand prince, prince, archduke, duke or grand duke, and in the Islamic world, malik, sultan, emir or hakim, among others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb